# --- end vendor verification

external:        File system placement and modes of the static content directories, which
                 decide what a reachable path can actually read, carried by the operating
                 system.
external:        MIME map entries added by third-party apps, carried by the app review
                 procedure (server.conf.spec:1656).

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000083 check and fix text;
                 web.conf.spec:333 (tools.staticdir.generate_indexes = [1 | 0], default 0),
                 web.conf.spec:308 (static_dir), web.conf.spec:303 (static_endpoint)
finding:         Splunk Web generates directory indexes for its static content, or declares
                 no static directory, so the application can return file types the hosted
                 views do not need.
